# Documentation placement

Canonical process: `docs/sdlc/lifecycle.md` (do not invent a second
lifecycle).

- `.cursor/rules/` = constraints
- `.cursor/skills/` = procedures; start with `feature-orchestrator`
- `docs/sdlc/` = lifecycle, DoR, DoD, risk, artifacts, change-control, roadmap
- `docs/product/` = product truth pointers
- `docs/features/<ID>/` = **new** feature packs (CRM-001+)
- AUTH-001 stays on existing `docs/requirements|specifications|user-stories|bdd|test-*|decisions` paths
- `docs/adr/` = platform ADRs only
- `docs/architecture/` = shared environment/architecture
- `docs/plans/TEMPLATE.md` = implementation plan template
- `src/` = application (not before PLANNED)

FS = WHAT. TS = HOW. ADR = WHY (platform). Plan = EXACTLY what files
change. Decision log = feature BD/TD until human accepts.

Unknowns: `TBD — HUMAN DECISION REQUIRED`.
